WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.541
ENO COMPTON: Let's
deploy a container

00:00:01.541 --> 00:00:02.620
to Google Compute Engine.

00:00:02.620 --> 00:00:05.474
To keep things simple, we will
deploy an nginx container.

00:00:05.474 --> 00:00:06.890
Before deploying
the container, we

00:00:06.890 --> 00:00:09.560
need to configure a firewall
rule to allow incoming HTTP

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:11.860
traffic on port 80.

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:13.277
We add a target
tag of HTTP server

00:00:13.277 --> 00:00:15.276
so we can associate our
container with this rule

00:00:15.276 --> 00:00:16.079
in the next step.

00:00:20.450 --> 00:00:21.980
The firewall rule
configured, we are

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:23.774
ready to deploy our container.

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:34.279
We'll name our VM nginx VM.

00:00:34.279 --> 00:00:36.070
We'll add the HTTP
server tag from the step

00:00:36.070 --> 00:00:38.800
before to associate the created
VM with the firewall rule,

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:40.640
and we will specify
our container image.

00:00:44.942 --> 00:00:46.470
The create-with-container
command

00:00:46.470 --> 00:00:48.480
starts a container using
the host's network.

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:51.060
This means we don't need to
provide any port mappings.

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:53.061
Now, let's test it.

00:00:53.061 --> 00:00:54.810
And with that, we have
a container running

00:00:54.810 --> 00:00:57.080
on Google Compute Engine.

